    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d368">

                <pb facs="0902" n="788" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg788"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Lot 60 D 224</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State’s Special Assistant</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Pasvolsky</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d368-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-08-18">August 18, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum for the Secretary</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Italian Documents</p>
                <p>The attached memoranda deal with the following questions: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Alternative methods of dealing with the Italo-Austrian and
                            Italo-Yugoslav <pb facs="0903" n="789" xml:id="pg789"/> frontiers; with
                            Italian colonial possessions; and with the island of Pantelleria.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Alternative methods of dealing with the internal political situation
                            in Italy, from the viewpoint of the problems of central and local
                            governments during the transitional period and later.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>The memoranda are accompanied by appropriate maps.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d368-f2"
                    /> They are based, in large measure, on discussions in various
                        committees.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d368-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>L[<hi rendition="#small-caps">eo</hi>] P[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >asvolsky</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
















